<newsitem itemid="118420" id="root" date="1996-10-15" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Tie Rack H1 pretax profit rises 23 pct.</title>
<headline>Tie Rack H1 pretax profit rises 23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>28 weeks to August 11</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.70		   vs 0.63</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.6		    vs 0.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.604		  vs 0.490</p>
<p> Turnover		   48.7		   vs 41.6</p>
<p> Operating result	 0.449		  vs 0.357</p>
<p> Interest		   0.304		  vs same</p>
<p> Tax			  0.223		  vs 0.174</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.381		  vs 0.316</p>
<p> Attributable	     0.365		  vs 0.322</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 14, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 10  Ex-div date		Dec 2</p>
<p>NOTE - Tie Rack, the ties retailer, said trading has continued generally satisfactory in the second half. The company expects a further 15 shops to be opened in the remainder of the year after the 22 were opened in 15 countries in the first half.</p>
<p>The firm now has 395 shops in 26 countries.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
